
While conventional macro-scale EM communication is very prevalent, Nano-scale EM based methods suffer from the same drawbacks which can be overcome at the macro-scale; viz. High Energy Requirements, and Fabrication. Materials dont hold up well together at the nano sclaes, therefore new, and better engineered methods are needed. For this, Various Different Elements are Used in Various Mixtures, Namely Carbon, DiElectric Moderate-Permittivity Gallium Nitride, High-Permittivity Hafnium Oxide, and Zinc Oxides. These New Materials Greatly Improve the Efficiency of The Nano-Antennas.

Along with more efficient Antennas, they also double as Energy Harvesters. As One of the most accessible and plentiful energy sources in real world phenomena is kinetic energy due to random vibrations in systems, Electrostatic Generators can provide us with energy density up to few microwatts to milliwats per unit volume.

As for the bandwidth of the channel, The Thz Band (0.1 to 10 Thz) is mainly used as lower frequency bands require large Antennas, which aren't possible at Nano-scales. This band is very popular for cellular networks as well, in 5G networks; As it can provide quite high communication speeds, However it has drawbacks in the form of high path loss, due to which it cannot travel long distances and needs highly directional Antennas, but it is not a problem for IoBNT applications as communication occurs at very short distances.

There is a problem however, this method of communication is very prone to Interference, which puts an upper bound on network capacity. This is Analysed Extensively by Yao in [23]. 

Fabrication is Analysed heavily in [26] with new Fabrication methods for sub 10nm nanogaps.




